WEBVTT

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:35.590
He shouldn't have visitors,
but you can have 10 minutes.

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:40.000
If his condition changes,
I'll have to ask you to leave.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.400
Understood.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.670
Tell us what happened there!

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.000
I don't know.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.300
How did it start?

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:49.170
I don't know.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:50.870
You must know!

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:53.010
You were part of the main staff!

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:55.110
It was my first time...

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:57.780
...being there.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.580
That's a lie!

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:02.550
Dr. Noguchi kept a file on the school server

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:04.280
about you for a year!

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:09.960
Come now, he just woke up.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:13.060
Perhaps he's merely confused.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.170
I'm going to start at the beginning, all right?

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:19.130
All right.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:21.700
First of all,

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:25.610
do you know what they
were trying to revive there?

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:26.580
Yes.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:27.880
It was an alien?

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.080
Yes.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:32.010
But the doctor went too quickly, right?

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.450
Curiosity got the better of him.

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:35.920
Excuse me, Colonel,

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.270
but aren't you leading the witness?

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:42.620
The thing is...

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:46.960
The thing is, there was an accident.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.780
There was a power surge.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:06.850
It overloaded the system.

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.520
And Maki was...

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:09.670
Maki was...

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.620
Maki was...

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.760
That's enough.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:13.920
Is that so?

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.270
Thank you.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.810
Forgive the intrusion, Takuto Kaneshiro.

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:24.700
Oh, by the way,

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.200
your team did a good job with the alien.

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:30.910
We know since we have it.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:37.750
Is this really fine?

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.820
He's not going anywhere injured like that.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:44.120
There's more than one way to pump a well.

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:18.380
Why the rush?

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:20.760
It's because of the generals.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.210
Well, what else is new?

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.260
How's the girl?

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:26.510
Still the same.

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:10.110
She's started to eat a little.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:11.070
Really?

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:13.140
We're letting Sue take care of her.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:16.630
Sue's still a child at heart, so they're getting along.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:21.320
What have you found to help us with the EX-1?

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:22.280
This.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:28.950
Harriet Bartholomew.
Born 2046. 13 years old.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:38.670
Family perished in a fire
during the first strike of 2054.

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:43.970
Home was burned to the ground,
but Harriet was rescued,

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:47.740
treated for shock for five years,

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:51.580
and recovered this year when she was sent...

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:54.380
...to live with her grandfather.

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:58.190
Right. She's had direct contact with the aliens.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.920
With the primary alien.

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.910
Oh, welcome back.

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:22.770
You're on the clock.

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:28.620
Jeez, cheap Japanese radio from the '70s.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:29.820
I see what you mean.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.220
A child at heart.

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:34.390
Where is she?

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:36.420
She hasn't left that spot.

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:44.600
Start the crane.

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:45.570
Starting.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:50.840
I hope Mr. Fairy is all right.

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:54.580
The generals want her.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.150
What do we do?

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:57.450
It can't be helped.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:07:00.350
Not until she says what she knows of the EX-1.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.550
That sounds pretty cruel.

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:06.490
Talking like that poor girl is a bag of rations.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:07.960
Enough, Lieutenant.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:09.530
But still...

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:10.490
Commander!

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:17.070
I've finished uploading those logs from the Morgue database.

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:18.100
Good work.

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:19.940
How was it at the hospital?

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:21.240
Not good.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.040
You talked to the survivor?

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:25.810
Then he was conscious?

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:29.610
No, his mind seemed to be scarred.

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:54.000
You look so sad.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.500
So sad.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:08:02.710
Is it that you can't recall or that you don't want to?

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:06.680
To turn away from the past is to lose it.

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:09.630
And parting is such sweet sorrow.

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:12.650
Who are you?

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:14.900
Don't like Shakespeare?

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:20.560
Forbidden fruit is the sweetest kind.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.430
What was it?

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:35.370
The thing that the army calls the EX-1?

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:37.150
You mean Frank?

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:38.610
That's it.

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:40.420
You'd like to kill him, right?

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:42.070
Or at least see him dead.

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:49.420
As Demetrius said, when two objects are equal in weight,

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:54.520
a simple speck of dust can make one heavier.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.950
Vengeance or clemency?

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:06.770
It's a difficult choice, that.

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:12.040
Which will you choose?

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:13.750
I...

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:25.430
Time to check your vitals, Mr. Kaneshiro.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:26.720
How do you feel?

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:30.930
Any change in your condition?

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:31.900
No.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:44.710
I'm here to take custody of the EX-1 and Harriet Bartholomew.

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:46.370
Please sign at the bottom.

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:48.510
Custody, huh?

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:58.060
Pressure destabilizing on number 3!

00:09:58.060 --> 00:09:59.130
What's wrong?

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:00.090
A wire's caught.

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:02.760
You have to shut it down!

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:14.110
Mr. Fairy!

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:15.510
Stand back!

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:16.670
Take out rope 4!

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.330
Good!

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:43.670
No!

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:58.880
Emergency stations!

00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:05.140
It's dangerous! Come over here!

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:41.160
Commander, are you hurt?

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:42.860
What happened to the EX-1?

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:52.970
I hate this. I can't take it.

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:57.950
Mr. Fairy, take me where
there aren't any scary noises.

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:00.610
Take me to the land of the fairies.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:21.640
What's the EX-1's position?

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:23.610
Flying low and slow.

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:25.440
Tracking's a snap.

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:27.210
It's making it easy.

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:28.130
Guess so.

00:12:28.130 --> 00:12:30.080
It must like the girl.

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:33.620
We just put the city on alert three minutes ago.

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:37.720
We told them there's an
alien air attack on the way.

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:39.700
Yes, that's the best tactic.

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:42.820
We need to catch it before the truth gets out.

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:45.590
It's up to us.

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:46.560
Roger.

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:05.740
I'm cold and hungry.

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:10.450
I'm all right, Mr. Fairy.

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:12.850
Let's get to your land.

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.650
I can put up with it.

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:26.840
It's changed course.

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:28.870
Heading into Garfield City.

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:30.120
Into the city?

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:33.270
What's he after so suddenly?

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:37.610
SARG 1, SARG 3, we have a situation.

00:13:37.610 --> 00:13:39.450
Prepare for manual take-off!

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:40.410
Roger!

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:06.410
SARG 1, SARG 3, separation confirmed.

00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:08.710
Monitoring positions.

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:10.710
Garfield City?

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:13.700
Is it heading for Takuto Kaneshiro in the hospital?

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:26.090
Is this the land of the fairies?

00:14:44.310 --> 00:14:46.640
No, no, no, no, no!

00:14:50.350 --> 00:14:52.190
No more, Mr. Fairy!

00:14:52.190 --> 00:14:54.460
This isn't the land of the fairies!

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:55.960
There's too many noises!

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:26.540
That's him! No question!

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:39.100
The army's behind schedule.

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:41.240
We'll have to go in without back up,

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:42.770
and stop the EX-1.

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:43.610
Can we?

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:44.570
Of course!

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:55.150
What?

00:16:22.340 --> 00:16:24.010
Those are weapons!

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:25.480
Those are ours?

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:27.040
Remarkable, aren't they?

00:16:28.350 --> 00:16:32.800
The SARG of the private
anti-alien combat unit Funeral.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:36.620
Superb, eh?

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:38.020
Beautiful, eh?

00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:42.400
State-of-the-art technological weaponry.

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:46.700
Come on, world, let's give them a hand!

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:47.670
Who are you?

00:17:00.550 --> 00:17:02.480
The girl's with it, after all.

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:04.750
It's got us in a corner.

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:06.760
It has the same problem.

00:17:06.760 --> 00:17:09.590
It won't move as long as she's with it.

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:11.060
As far as I can see.

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:18.500
It's getting away!

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:20.170
Keep it on the ground!

00:17:20.170 --> 00:17:22.070
The army will be there soon!

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:23.870
But...

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:25.100
I'll go after it!

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:37.850
This is no time for piggyback rides.

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:40.820
The hospital's ahead!

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:41.790
I know that!

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:45.890
Dan!

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:50.700
Not enough power!

00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:51.770
No!

00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:53.230
Don't release the limiter!

00:17:53.230 --> 00:17:56.430
Do you want to skip a grade ahead of your time like him?

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:58.390
Then what should I do?

00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:07.920
Excuse me.

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:11.390
Good.

00:18:11.390 --> 00:18:13.320
Now we can keep our distance.

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:14.520
What are you doing?

00:18:14.520 --> 00:18:16.320
I'll show you how to fish.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:17.660
Parallax on.

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.260
Calculate distance.

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:21.860
Allowing for wind resistance.

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:30.870
No!

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:39.900
Maki!

00:18:39.900 --> 00:18:42.500
<i>Where springs become summers...</i>

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:43.520
Maki!

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:43.750
<i>...and green meadows lie.</i>

00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:45.250
Maki!

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:45.920
<i>...and green meadows lie.</i>

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:49.460
Stop!

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:51.260
Stop it!

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:04.510
Maki!

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:08.380
It's me!

00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:09.340
I'm right here!

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:12.740
Who are you?

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:16.380
Are you a fairy, too?

00:19:22.360 --> 00:19:24.260
I'm not...

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:25.260
...me.

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.710
I should've known.

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:30.200
This isn't it.

00:19:31.130 --> 00:19:34.970
This isn't the land of the fairies.

00:19:40.580 --> 00:19:42.380
P-Please wait!

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:51.620
It's okay, Mr. Fairy.

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:55.770
There really isn't a land of fairies anywhere, right?

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:01.660
You don't have to look for it anymore.

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:05.870
My dad, my mom, and my grandpa left.

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:08.670
And if you left, too...

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:10.800
So...

00:20:19.850 --> 00:20:21.650
Shame we had to do it.

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:28.450
But if this girl can really
communicate with the EX-1...

00:20:37.930 --> 00:20:38.960
Come out.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:41.140
You're there, right?

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:44.510
Your wish is my command, master.

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:47.310
The Genie of the Lamp is at your service.

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:48.500
I...

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:53.980
If I could destroy him with my own hands...

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:56.780
...I don't care what happens to me.

00:20:58.620 --> 00:21:01.420
Very commendable.

00:21:01.420 --> 00:21:02.760
But you know,

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:09.260
the way a devil wins trust
is by playing the part of an angel.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:13.190
You don't believe I'm an angel, do you?

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:14.930
Devil or angel,

00:21:15.700 --> 00:21:17.470
it doesn't matter.

00:21:17.470 --> 00:21:19.370
Very well, it's your choice.

00:21:20.440 --> 00:21:24.450
"And from the darkness of hell a demon arose...

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:27.250
...to lead them to corruption."

00:21:29.320 --> 00:21:30.790
Sleep.

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:32.790
Turn away from the light.

00:21:32.790 --> 00:21:35.590
What are you anyway?

00:21:35.590 --> 00:21:38.750
An interested third party, I suppose.

00:21:45.870 --> 00:21:47.420
Are you awake?

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:49.700
U-Uh...

00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:52.910
Dr. Butch, please.

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:55.580
Mr. Ryu Soma is awake.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:56.680
Ryu...

00:21:56.680 --> 00:21:57.880
...Soma?

00:21:57.880 --> 00:22:02.020
That's right. The one from the car accident last night.

00:22:02.020 --> 00:22:03.280
Right.

00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:06.380
Mr. Soma, the doctor is on his way to see you.

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:08.950
Mr. Soma?

00:22:11.730 --> 00:22:14.700
Are you sure about this, Mr. Soma?

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:17.530
Reconstructive surgery is quite painless.

00:22:17.530 --> 00:22:18.600
I'm sure.

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:20.300
This is fine.

00:22:21.140 --> 00:22:23.640
A fairy, huh?

00:22:35.820 --> 00:22:39.170
Is a devil or an angel guiding me?

00:22:40.490 --> 00:22:45.150
Sometimes, hatred is the only thing a man has to live for.

00:22:46.490 --> 00:22:49.190
Next time,
The Meeting and Hatred.
